Safety PLC (golden Jason 20230619: Gerneral.ini [System] SafePlcIO, Modbus TCP 172.16.8.120:502, input registers 30001-30022): before this TPLCIOThread::Resume() was a no-op (nothing pumped PLCIOProcess) and PlcComm was a SIM socket. New MyPLC/SafePlcClock_St02.cpp: with SafePlcIO=1 a FastClock 'safeplc' 1 ms kDelay job (= golden Synchronize(PLCIOProcess) + MySleepEx(1)) runs PlcComm.W906_Poll() (the socket events on this thread, as golden's message loop) and then golden PLCIOProcess verbatim; PlcComm switched to vclcompat POLLED-Real (new ModbusTCPClient::W906_UsePolledRealSocket / W906_Poll), re-opened if InitPLCIO already opened it in SIM; one [SAFEPLC] stdout line per connection change / first data. FastClockWbServe.cpp registers it (same line as the pad job), CMakeLists adds the file (same line), cinitial GATE (W7a-I3) note updated (same line). SafePlcIO stays 0 on this machine: the PLC answers (ping, TCP 502, read-only FC4) but all 22 bytes read 0 and a 20-minute watch saw no bit change; IO_Table has no SnAllEMG / SnAllSafeDoor (ISABase 4) rows -- turning it on now would raise WAR16140 constantly.

Machine data (not in this repo, pushed by push_stage's machine_params snapshot): Gerneral.ini ControlPanelMode 0->1, [TrayY] COM PORT COM18->COM4, [NUMBER_PANEL2] COM_PORT COM4->COM14 (backup Gerneral.ini.bak_panel_20261006_152525); Error\AlarmCodeList.txt + WAR16154 (backup .bak_war16154_20261006_153942).

o2 full build 0 errors; ctest 380/400 (HSys_HeaterMix / SetTempSave failed under -j6, both pass alone; the rest = the known list); production_audit overlapped EastSun's F5 (booted 15:32), changes are the program's own; Debug and release wb_serve rebuilt. WORKLOG item 134.

